DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The   wwccssnnlleenn()  function  is  the  wide‐character  equivalent  of  the
       ssttrrnnlleenn(3) function.  It returns the number of wide‐characters  in  the
       string pointed to by _s, not including the terminating null wide charac‐
       ter  (L'\0'),  but at most _m_a_x_l_e_n wide characters (note: this parameter
       is not a byte count).  In doing this, wwccssnnlleenn() looks at only the first
       _m_a_x_l_e_n wide characters at _s and never beyond _s_[_m_a_x_l_e_n_-_1_].

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       The wwccssnnlleenn() function returns _w_c_s_l_e_n_(_s_), if that is less than  _m_a_x_l_e_n,
       or  _m_a_x_l_e_n  if  there  is no null wide character among the first _m_a_x_l_e_n
       wide characters pointed to by _s.

